A2065 Ethernet and uaenet.device on WinUAE's built-in SLIRP (Windows)

A2065, SANA2, WITH_SLIRP and WITH_BUILTIN_SLIRP were undefined and SLIRP's sources were not in
the build. The card and the SANA-II device are built already; this gives them a network: SLIRP,
a user-mode NAT inside the emulator (the Amiga is 10.0.2.15, gateway 10.0.2.2 = the host's
loopback, DNS 10.0.2.3, DHCP), which needs no driver or privileges on the host.

Windows only: slirp_uae.c's receive loop and SLIRP's socket layer are WinUAE's Winsock code
(INT_PTR descriptors, select() without nfds), and this was built and tested on Windows alone.
The defines are under _WIN32 and the sources under a Windows platform check, so other builds
are unchanged.

- sysconfig.h: A2065, SANA2, WITH_SLIRP, WITH_BUILTIN_SLIRP on Windows.
- Makefile.common: slirp_uae.c and slirp/*.cpp (C++, as in WinUAE) on Windows.
- slirp/packed.h, slirp/unpacked.h (new): missing from the tree; they bracket the wire-format
  structs, unpacked.h supplying the declaration's closing PACKED__;.
- slirp/libslirp.h: C linkage for the entry points (called from C slirp_uae.c) and for
  slirp_output(), which ethernet.c defines in C.
- slirp/slirp.cpp: slirp_select_fill() takes INT_PTR *, as libslirp.h declares; with int, C++
  made it a second overload and the C caller did not link.
- slirp/slirp.h: no <sys/ioctl.h> on Windows (sysconfig.h sets HAVE_SYS_IOCTL_H everywhere), and
  container_of() for GCC, not only MSVC.
- slirp/cksum.cpp: cksum() returns u_short, as slirp.h declares.
- slirp_uae.c: a typedef for enum Implementation, so it compiles as C.
- cfgfile.c, ethernet.c: winsock2.h/arpa/inet.h under WITH_SLIRP for inet_addr and in_addr.
- ethernet.c: stubs for the NE2000-family boards (Ariadne II, Hydra, LAN Rover, X-Surf), whose
  qemuvga/ne2000.c is not built; the same stubs the build without SLIRP already had.
- uaenet.c, include/uaenet.h: the pcap backend needs WITH_UAENET_PCAP as well as A2065.
- libretro-glue.c: target_ethernet_enumerate() lists the drivers, as WinUAE's target does. It
  returned NULL, so every driver name became "no selection" and a2065_config's
  ethernet_enumerate(&td, romtype) took the list-everything branch, writing three pointers into
  the one static - overwriting sysdata, which the reset then frees.
- libretro-core.c: puae_a2065 (disabled, slirp, slirp_inbound - which also forwards host ports
  21-23 and 80) writes a2065_rom_file=:ENABLED and a2065_rom_options=<driver>, the rows WinUAE
  writes (a2065= alone only enables the card, and the _rom_file row is what makes the parser
  list the driver names before it reads the options); puae_sana2 (disabled/enabled) writes
  sana2=true. Both options are declared only when the core has A2065/SANA2.

Applies to libretro-uae 2b0ed42fe565fb997a0627aaa8f44e0948b527f8 in the order given by
patches/series.txt.

